@smarterclayton this means that dates will be normalized when reserialized, and will appear to have changed format from the client's perspective.

While this already happens in some cases (like resource.Quantity handling), it also causes problems (xref https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/106388 where writing a non-normalized quantity value can trigger managedFields timestamp updates and etcd writes even when no other serialized value changed).

Do we want to open up the same issues for microtime?
